lemma=\"NOLEMMA\">CE</span>[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]<span data-text=\"Caius\" data-n=\"105\" data-lemma=\"Gaius\">CAIUS</span><span data-text=\"Iulius\" data-n=\"115\" data-lemma=\"Iulius\">IULIUS</span><span data-text=\"Pr\" data-n=\"125\" data-lemma=\"NOLEMMA\">PR</span>[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]PAISV[<span dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---</span>]</span></div><p class=\"miniapp\"></p></div></div>  <div id=\"facsimile-images\"><h2>Facsimile Images</h2></div>  <div id=\"apparatus\"><h4>Apparatus criticus</h4><ul><li><span>  <span>Text of Mommsen (from autopsy)</span>  </span>; </li><li><span class=\"3\">3: <span>Amico: DIOP...</span>  </span><br></li><li><span class=\"4\">4: <span>Amico: CEI...</span>  </span><br></li><li><span class=\"6\">6: <span>Amico: CRASSVS...</span>  </span></li></ul></div>  <div id=\"translation\"><h2> translation</h2><p class=\"translation-author\">  </p><p>  </p></div>  <div id=\"commentary\"><h2>commentary</h2>  <p>Manganaro and Korhonen suggest that this might be a list of officials; Amico assumed it to be a list of those buried in a tomb and so funerary, since the area of its discovery is more broadly that of the necropolis.</p>  </div>  <div id=\"bibliography\"><h2>bibliography</h2>  <ul><li> Amico 1741 224 no. 28 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002186\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002186</a>  </li><li> Castelli 1769 cl. XVIII no. 47 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002084\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002084</a>  </li><li> Castelli 1784 cl. XVIII no. 48 <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002083\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002083</a>  </li><li> Mommsen 1883 <a href=\"http://arachne.uni-koeln.de/item/buchseite/650759\" target=\"_blank\">7044</a>  <a href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000589\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000589</a>